<section class="feature-strip" aria-label="Key Specifications">
  <div class="feature-item">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
      <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
    </svg>
    <span>Real-Time Clock Sync</span>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-item">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
      <line x1="16" y1="2" x2="16" y2="6"></line>
      <line x1="8" y1="2" x2="8" y2="6"></line>
      <line x1="3" y1="10" x2="21" y2="10"></line>
    </svg>
    <span>DST Transition Detection</span>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-item">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <polygon points="3 6 9 3 15 6 21 3 21 18 15 21 9 18 3 21"></polygon>
      <line x1="9" y1="3" x2="9" y2="18"></line>
      <line x1="15" y1="6" x2="15" y2="21"></line>
    </svg>
    <span>IANA Database Standards</span>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     1. CONVERT GMT TO EST INSTANTLY
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="convert-instantly">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Instant Calculation</div>
    <h2>Convert GMT to EST Instantly</h2>
    <p>
      Our synchronization engine converts Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) to Eastern Standard Time (EST) or Eastern Daylight Time (EDT) dynamically in the browser. Unlike static calculators that fail during seasonal clock changes, this tool processes conversions using timezone parameters. Select your preferred date, enter the source time, and retrieve the translated value instantly.
    </p>
    <p>
      This platform helps you convert <strong>GMT to Eastern Time</strong> without errors. By analyzing active regional rules, the system resolves offsets, ensuring your business schedules, gaming events, and international flights match local clocks.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     2. CURRENT GMT AND EST TIME
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="clock-grid reveal" id="current-clocks">
  <h2 style="grid-column: 1 / -1; margin-bottom: 8px;">Current GMT and EST Time</h2>
  
  <div class="clock-card">
    <span class="eyebrow">Greenwich Mean Time Clock</span>
    <strong id="gmtClock">--:--:-- GMT</strong>
    <p>UTC+0 Base Meridian</p>
  </div>

  <div class="clock-card">
    <span class="eyebrow">Eastern Time Clock (New York)</span>
    <strong id="estClock">--:--:-- ET</strong>
    <p>Active Offset: <em id="estZone">ET</em></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     3. WHY GMT AND EST ARE DIFFERENT
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="why-different">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Geographic Separation</div>
    <h2>Why GMT and EST Are Different</h2>
    <p>
      Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) and Eastern Standard Time (EST) differ because of the Earth's physical rotation and longitudinal distance. The planet completes a 360-degree rotation every 24 hours, meaning every 15 degrees of longitude represents one hour of solar travel. The Prime Meridian (0° longitude) runs through Greenwich, England, which establishes the zero-hour offset.
    </p>
    <p>
      In contrast, the East Coast of North America is situated approximately 75 degrees west of the Prime Meridian. This physical distance places the Eastern timezone five hours behind the solar time of Greenwich. Consequently, when the sun is directly overhead in London, the East Coast of the United States and Canada is just starting its morning hours.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     4. GMT VS EST EXPLAINED
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="gmt-vs-est-explained">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Standard Clarifications</div>
    <h2>GMT vs EST Explained</h2>
    <p>
      Understanding the distinction between Greenwich Mean Time and Eastern Standard Time requires separating astronomical designations from political standards. GMT represents a time standard historically determined by the Royal Observatory in Greenwich. It does not adjust for daylight saving, making it a constant timezone baseline.
    </p>
    <p>
      EST is a specific offset (UTC-5) observed by North American jurisdictions during winter. When people search for <strong>gmt to est converter</strong>, they are often referring to Eastern Time (ET) in general, which changes seasonally. It is critical to differentiate between the standard winter offset (EST) and the daylight summer offset (EDT) to avoid scheduling discrepancies.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     5. GMT TO EST TIME DIFFERENCE
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="time-difference">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Offset Gaps</div>
    <h2>GMT to EST Time Difference</h2>
    <p>
      The absolute time difference between Greenwich Mean Time and Eastern Time transitions between two distinct offsets every year. During standard time, which operates in the winter months, the difference is exactly five hours (GMT is five hours ahead of EST). During daylight saving time, the difference is reduced to four hours (GMT is four hours ahead of EDT).
    </p>
    <p>
      This seasonal variance creates scheduling issues for organizations operating across the Atlantic. For instance, a meeting scheduled at 3:00 PM GMT translates to 10:00 AM EST in December, but shifts to 11:00 AM EDT in June. Utilizing a date-aware converter is the only way to safeguard your operations against these variations.
    </p>
  </div>
  
  <!-- ILLUSTRATION 1: GMT VS EST TIMELINE -->
  <div class="hero-visual" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 24px auto 0;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 220" width="100%" height="auto" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0c354a 0%, #12455d 100%); border-radius: 8px;">
      <text x="400" y="40" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">GMT VS EST TIMELINE & OFFSET RELATIONSHIP</text>
      <line x1="100" y1="120" x2="700" y2="120" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="4" />
      
      <!-- GMT Node -->
      <circle cx="200" cy="120" r="12" fill="#36c7b5" stroke="#0c354a" stroke-width="3" />
      <text x="200" y="90" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">Greenwich Mean Time (GMT)</text>
      <text x="200" y="155" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">UTC+0 Baseline Meridian</text>
      
      <!-- EST Node -->
      <circle cx="600" cy="120" r="12" fill="#8fd7ff" stroke="#0c354a" stroke-width="3" />
      <text x="600" y="90" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">Eastern Standard Time (EST)</text>
      <text x="600" y="155" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">UTC-5 Winter Offset</text>

      <!-- Offset Bracket -->
      <path d="M 200 120 L 200 140 L 600 140 L 600 120" fill="none" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.6" />
      <text x="400" y="185" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">5-Hour Standard Time Gap</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     6. GMT TO EST DAYLIGHT SAVING RULES
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="daylight-rules">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">DST Legislation</div>
    <h2>GMT to EST Daylight Saving Rules</h2>
    <p>
      Daylight Saving Time (DST) rules in the Eastern timezone are defined by national energy laws. In the United States and Canada, DST starts on the second Sunday of March and ends on the first Sunday of November. During these dates, clocks in cities like New York and Toronto move forward one hour, changing the timezone designation from EST (UTC-5) to EDT (UTC-4).
    </p>
    <p>
      Crucially, the United Kingdom and continental Europe change their clocks on different dates—specifically on the last Sunday of March and the last Sunday of October. This creates a two-to-three week transition window in spring and autumn where the relative offset shifts to 4 hours or 6 hours. Our database-aware calculator handles these transition anomalies seamlessly.
    </p>
  </div>
  
  <!-- ILLUSTRATION 2: DST INFOGRAPHIC -->
  <div class="hero-visual" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 24px auto 0;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 220" width="100%" height="auto" style="background: #0f172a; border-radius: 8px;">
      <text x="400" y="35" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">EASTERN TIME DST TRANSITIONS (ANNUAL CALENDAR)</text>
      
      <!-- Spring Block -->
      <g transform="translate(80, 60)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="280" height="110" rx="8" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="140" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">Spring Forward (March)</text>
        <text x="140" y="55" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Second Sunday of March at 2:00 AM</text>
        <text x="140" y="75" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">Clocks shift forward: EST -> EDT</text>
        <text x="140" y="95" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">New Offset: UTC-4 (4h behind GMT)</text>
      </g>
      
      <!-- Autumn Block -->
      <g transform="translate(440, 60)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="280" height="110" rx="8" fill="#1b536e" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="140" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Fall Back (November)</text>
        <text x="140" y="55" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">First Sunday of November at 2:00 AM</text>
        <text x="140" y="75" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">Clocks shift backward: EDT -> EST</text>
        <text x="140" y="95" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">New Offset: UTC-5 (5h behind GMT)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     7. GMT TO EST INTERACTIVE CONVERTER
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="hero reveal" id="converter">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow">Interactive Converter</div>
    <h2>GMT to EST Interactive Converter</h2>
    <p>
      To convert Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) to Eastern Standard Time (EST) or Eastern Daylight Time (EDT), utilize our live form below. You can toggle between timezone directions using the swap button, lock in your current local time, and copy output strings directly to your clipboard.
    </p>
    <p>
      The logic utilizes native browser APIs and queries the active OS database locale to ensure calculations are correct for whatever calendar date you select.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <Converter intent="converter" t={t} context={context} />
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     8. 24 HOUR GMT TO EST TABLE
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="reveal" id="conversion-table">
  <h2>24 Hour GMT to EST Table</h2>
  <p>
    This comparative index maps every hour of Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) to Eastern Standard Time (EST) and Eastern Daylight Time (EDT), highlighting the changes in offset during seasonal transitions. Use this index to review full-day comparisons at a glance.
  </p>
  
  <div class="table-container" style="overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);">
          <th style="padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; color: var(--accent);">GMT (UTC+0)</th>
