<section class="source-notes reveal" id="final-summary">
  <h2>Final Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Converting **GMT to EST** requires understanding the seasonal transitions of North American Eastern Time. During the winter, the region observes Eastern Standard Time (EST) at a five-hour offset (UTC-5). During the summer, it observes Eastern Daylight Time (EDT) at a four-hour offset (UTC-4). Utilizing a date-aware timezone converter ensures schedules are computed accurately, avoiding missed connections.
  </p>
